## 4. Routing and Route Tables

### Transit Gateway Route Tables

Transit Gateway uses separate route tables for organizing traffic flow.

```bash
# List route tables
aws ec2 describe-transit-gateway-route-tables \
  --filters "Name=transit-gateway-id,Values=$TGW" \
  --query 'TransitGatewayRouteTables[*].[TransitGatewayRouteTableId,State,Tags[?Key==`Name`].Value|[0]]' \
  --output table

# Response:
# tgw-rtb-prod-prod    available  prod-route-table
# tgw-rtb-dev-dev      available  dev-route-table
# tgw-rtb-shared-shar  available  shared-route-table
```

### Create Segmented Route Tables

```bash
# Create Production Route Table
PROD_RT=$(aws ec2 create-transit-gateway-route-table \
  --transit-gateway-id $TGW \
  --tag-specifications 'ResourceType=transit-gateway-route-table,Tags=[{Key=Name,Value=prod-routes}]' \
  --query 'TransitGatewayRouteTable.TransitGatewayRouteTableId' \
  --output text)

# Create Development Route Table
DEV_RT=$(aws ec2 create-transit-gateway-route-table \
  --transit-gateway-id $TGW \
  --tag-specifications 'ResourceType=transit-gateway-route-table,Tags=[{Key=Name,Value=dev-routes}]' \
  --query 'TransitGatewayRouteTable.TransitGatewayRouteTableId' \
  --output text)

# Create Shared Route Table (for services)
SHARED_RT=$(aws ec2 create-transit-gateway-route-table \
  --transit-gateway-id $TGW \
  --tag-specifications 'ResourceType=transit-gateway-route-table,Tags=[{Key=Name,Value=shared-routes}]' \
  --query 'TransitGatewayRouteTable.TransitGatewayRouteTableId' \
  --output text)

echo "Route Tables Created:"
echo "Production: $PROD_RT"
echo "Development: $DEV_RT"
echo "Shared: $SHARED_RT"
```

### Associate Attachments to Route Tables

```bash
# Associate VPC attachment to Production route table
aws ec2 associate-transit-gateway-route-table \
  --transit-gateway-route-table-id $PROD_RT \
  --transit-gateway-attachment-id $VPC_ATTACHMENT

# Associate attachment to route table means:
# - VPC attachment will use this route table
# - Routes in table determine where traffic goes
# - Can only have one route table per attachment
```

### Create Routes

```bash
# Static route: On-premises via Direct Connect
aws ec2 create-transit-gateway-route \
  --transit-gateway-route-table-id $PROD_RT \
  --destination-cidr-block 10.0.0.0/8 \
  --transit-gateway-attachment-id $DX_ATTACHMENT

# Route to another VPC
aws ec2 create-transit-gateway-route \
  --transit-gateway-route-table-id $PROD_RT \
  --destination-cidr-block 10.1.0.0/16 \
  --transit-gateway-attachment-id $VPC2_ATTACHMENT

# Blackhole route (block traffic)
aws ec2 create-transit-gateway-route \
  --transit-gateway-route-table-id $PROD_RT \
  --destination-cidr-block 192.168.0.0/16 \
  --blackhole

# List routes
aws ec2 search-transit-gateway-routes \
  --transit-gateway-route-table-id $PROD_RT \
  --query 'Routes[*].[DestinationCidrBlock,Type,State,TransitGatewayAttachments[0].TransitGatewayAttachmentId]' \
  --output table
```

