## 5. Route Propagation

Route propagation automatically adds routes based on attachment advertisements.

### Enable Route Propagation

```bash
# Enable propagation for attachment
aws ec2 enable-transit-gateway-route-table-propagation \
  --transit-gateway-route-table-id $PROD_RT \
  --transit-gateway-attachment-id $VPC_ATTACHMENT

# Result:
# VPC attachment automatically advertises its CIDR block (10.1.0.0/16)
# Route added to PROD_RT: 10.1.0.0/16 → VPC attachment

# For Direct Connect (BGP learned routes):
aws ec2 enable-transit-gateway-route-table-propagation \
  --transit-gateway-route-table-id $PROD_RT \
  --transit-gateway-attachment-id $DX_ATTACHMENT

# Result:
# All on-premises routes (10.0.0.0/8) automatically propagated
# No manual route creation needed for DX or on-prem additions
```

### Disable Route Propagation

```bash
# Disable propagation (removes auto-learned routes)
aws ec2 disable-transit-gateway-route-table-propagation \
  --transit-gateway-route-table-id $PROD_RT \
  --transit-gateway-attachment-id $VPC_ATTACHMENT

# Use case:
# - Prevent route advertisements
# - Enforce static routing only
# - Isolate development environment
```

