## 6. Multi-Region Connectivity

### Regional Architecture

```
US-East-1 Region:
┌──────────────────────┐
│   Transit Gateway    │
│    (tgw-us-east)     │
├──────────────────────┤
│  ├─ VPC-1 (Prod)    │
│  ├─ VPC-2 (Dev)     │
│  └─ DX Attachment   │
└──────────────────────┘
         │
         │ (Peering Link)
         │
         ↓
EU-West-1 Region:
┌──────────────────────┐
│   Transit Gateway    │
│    (tgw-eu-west)     │
├──────────────────────┤
│  ├─ VPC-3 (Prod)    │
│  ├─ VPC-4 (Dev)     │
│  └─ DX Attachment   │
└──────────────────────┘
```

### Enable Multi-Region Routing

```bash
# Create peering attachment (from us-east-1)
PEERING=$(aws ec2 create-transit-gateway-peering-attachment \
  --transit-gateway-id tgw-us-east-1 \
  --peer-transit-gateway-id tgw-eu-west-1 \
  --peer-account-id 123456789012 \
  --peer-region eu-west-1 \
  --region us-east-1 \
  --query 'TransitGatewayPeeringAttachment.TransitGatewayAttachmentId' \
  --output text)

echo "Peering Attachment (pending): $PEERING"

# Accept peering (in eu-west-1)
aws ec2 accept-transit-gateway-peering-attachment \
  --transit-gateway-attachment-id $PEERING \
  --region eu-west-1

# Create route in us-east-1 route table to eu-west-1 networks
aws ec2 create-transit-gateway-route \
  --transit-gateway-route-table-id tgw-rtb-us-east-prod \
  --destination-cidr-block 10.100.0.0/16 \
  --transit-gateway-attachment-id $PEERING \
  --region us-east-1

# Enable propagation for multi-region discovery
aws ec2 enable-transit-gateway-route-table-propagation \
  --transit-gateway-route-table-id tgw-rtb-us-east-prod \
  --transit-gateway-attachment-id $PEERING \
  --region us-east-1
```

